createdby: DBot
description: Removes one or more entities from a GCP Cloud Storage bucket's Access
  Control List (ACL). Use this action to remediate publicly exposed buckets by removing
  the 'allUsers' entity (which makes the bucket accessible to anyone on the internet)
  or 'allAuthenticatedUsers' (which makes it accessible to any Google account holder).
  Can also revoke access for specific users or groups by removing user, group, or
  domain entities. This is a remediation action that modifies bucket access permissions.
  REQUIRES `project_id` and `resource_name`; if not in user input, resolve them first
  via `CortexListAssets` using the issue's asset_id or asset_name.
